>From grow_up() in makemon.c (excerpted harshly):

    if (victim) {           /* killed a monster */
        lev_limit = 3 * (int)ptr->mlevel / 2;
    } else {
       /* a gain level potion or wraith corpse; always go up a level
          unless already at maximum (49 is hard upper limit except
          for demon lords, who start at 50 and can't go any higher) */
        lev_limit = 50;             /* recalc below */
    }
    if (is_mplayer(ptr)) lev_limit = 30;    /* same as player */
    else if (lev_limit < 5) lev_limit = 5;  /* arbitrary */
    else if (lev_limit > 49) lev_limit = (ptr->mlevel > 49 ? 50 : 49);

Note that growing into a different version of the monster takes
precedence over this limit.

(If you want to go this route, you'll also need to work out the "real"
base level of the named demons; from makemon():

   } else if (ptr->mlevel > 49) {
        /* "special" fixed hp monster
         * the hit points are encoded in the mlevel in a somewhat strange
         * way to fit in the 50..127 positive range of a signed character
         * above the 1..49 that indicate "normal" monster levels */
        mtmp->mhpmax = mtmp->mhp = 2*(ptr->mlevel - 6);
        mtmp->m_lev = mtmp->mhp / 4;        /* approximation */

and adj_lev():

   if((tmp = ptr->mlevel) > 49) return(50); /* "special" demons/devils */

Or you could just grab the figures from Ali Harlow's Monster Manual,
since there's no point in duplicating any more of his work than you
have already.)

